One of the distinctive things about YC as compared to later stage investors is that you have to be prepared to give advice about practically everything. Names, logos, features, hiring, visas, LOIs, ads, investor pitches, and even when to ditch the idea.

Fortunately because you fund such a large number of startups in the earliest stage, the YC partners also get the most practice in dealing with problems. Every quarter there are 250 complete new sets of problems.

When you fund startups on that scale, there's practically no lag time between some new type of problem arising and the partners becoming aware of it. If there's a new type of problem, there will be 5 startups in the current batch with it.

